======================================================================
RECOMMENDED HANDLING (grouped by strategy)
======================================================================

[CATEGORY_NOT_MEASURED]  (2 columns)
  max_glu_serum, A1Cresult
  -> NaN = test not performed; fill with 'Not measured'.

[DROP_HIGH_MISSING]  (1 columns)
  weight
  -> 96.9% missing — too sparse to impute.

[DROP_ID]  (2 columns)
  encounter_id, patient_nbr
  -> Identifier / leakage risk — exclude from features.

[DROP_ZERO_VARIANCE]  (15 columns)
  nateglinide, chlorpropamide, acetohexamide, tolbutamide, acarbose, miglitol, troglitazone, tolazamide, examide, citoglipton, glyburide-metformin, glipizide-metformin, glimepiride-pioglitazone, metformin-rosiglitazone, metformin-pioglitazone
  -> One value covers 99.31% of rows — no signal.

[IMPUTE_CATEGORY]  (6 columns)
  race, payer_code, medical_specialty, diag_1, diag_2, diag_3
  -> Fill missing with an explicit 'Unknown' category.

[OK]  (24 columns)
  gender, age, admission_type_id, discharge_disposition_id, admission_source_id, time_in_hospital, num_lab_procedures, num_procedures, num_medications, number_outpatient, number_emergency, number_inpatient, number_diagnoses, metformin, repaglinide, glimepiride, glipizide, glyburide, pioglitazone, rosiglitazone, insulin, change, diabetesMed, readmitted
  -> Complete — usable as-is.

======================================================================
DUPLICATE / LEAKAGE CHECK
======================================================================
  duplicate_encounter_id          : 0
  patients_with_repeat_encounters : 30,248
  unique_patients                 : 71,518
  total_encounters                : 101,766

  Note: ~30k encounters are repeat visits by the same patient.
  Consider keeping only the first encounter per patient_nbr, or use
  patient-grouped splits, to avoid train/test leakage.

======================================================================
INVALID CATEGORY VALUES
======================================================================
  gender == 'Unknown/Invalid'     : 3

